  <data name="FogMultiplierLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fog density multiplier</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FogMultiplierLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scales all fog densities with the given multiplier.&#x0a;&#x0a;Recommended ranges:&#x0a;0.2–0.8 for lighter fog&#x0a;1.5-3.0 for dense fog&#x0a;0.0 to disable air fog&#x0a;&#x0a;Advanced tip: The value of the multiplier will be treated as, and applied, as a literal density value if fog density is already too small (like 0) to multiply.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="EmissivityMultiplierLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Emissive strength multiplier</value>
  </data>
  <data name="EmissivityMultiplierLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scales glowing effects of all emissive blocks.&#x0a;&#x0a;Examples:&#x0a;1 = default&#x0a;0.5 = half brightness&#x0a;higher values = stronger glowing effects on blocks.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="AmbientLightLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Increase ambient lighting</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AmbientLightLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Modifies ambient lighting when emissivity is adjusted, higher emissive multipliers strengthen the effect.&#x0a;&#x0a;Note: Applying this option to a resource pack will block Emissive multiplier from being applied to that resource pack ever again unless the resource pack is reset/reinstalled freshly.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="EmissivityAmbientLightToggle.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Automation]AutomationProperties.Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Emissivity Ambient Light Toggle</value>
  </data>
  <data name="EmissivityWarningIcon.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enabling this option while tuning a resource pack will cause future tuning attempts to skip applying the Emissivity Multiplier slider to that pack, this intentional guardrail keeps PBR from appearing broken.&#x0a;Furthermore, this option is intended for RTX resource packs only, do not enable for Vibrant Visuals resource packs. Use this option sparingly or as the last step in tuning a resource pack to your taste.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="NormalIntensityLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Surface 3D effect intensity</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NormalIntensityLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Adjust intensity of normal maps, heightmaps, and parallax occlusion mapping in percentage, if available.&#x0a;&#x0a;0% = flattens all textures&#x0a;100% = default (no change)&#x0a;Higher values = stronger 3D effects on surfaces.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="MaterialNoiseLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Material grain offset</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MaterialNoiseLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Adds additional detail to PBR textures and reduces uniformity by adding a layer of noise to PBR textures, impacts mid-range values harder and extreme values less. Impacts emissives less than roughness and metalness properties.&#x0a;Your input determines the maximum possible deviation from the original values.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="RoughenUpLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Roughness control</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RoughenUpLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Adjusts overall balance of roughness and metalness of materials.&#x0a;&#x0a;Higher values result in overall fewer or weaker glossy surfaces and metallic metals&#x0a;Negative values strengthen glossy or metallic surfaces.&#x0a;Uses a smart decaying curve to impact extreme values that are relevant. Keeps each texture's composition/relative values intact.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="LazifyNormalsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Lazify surface normals</value>
  </data>
  <data name="LazifyNormalsLabel.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Lazifies heightmaps and normal maps by reducing refinedness.&#x0a;&#x0a;0 = no change&#x0a;255 = fully lazy&#x0a;Resource packs that are already shoddy might see no change or even slight improvements, while higher quality packs can receive an additional layer of detail, for which a small value under 20 is generally recommended.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="TuneSelectionButton.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Begins permanently modifying all of the selected packs using the current set of parameters above.&#x0a;&#x0a;Ensure Minecraft is closed while packs are being tuned to avoid issues; Or at the very least reload your world to see the changes take effect.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExportButtonText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Export</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExportButton.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exports selected packages as .mcpack for creating backups or easy sharing.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DeleteButton.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Physically delete the files of the selected packages from game's data directory.&#x0a;&#x0a;WARNING FOR ADVANCED USERS: This functionality walks up to the parent directory of the selected resource pack, as to not leave orphaned empty folders behind, if you keep other files inside a resource pack, or keep multiple resource packs inside one folder for whatever the reason, steer clear of this button.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="LaunchPackUpdateButton.[using:Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
